			"Message": "save\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>",
			"SHA": "3d2b28aefc799d19721540a9ae96808c909f9321"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-05T13:40:52Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				670,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): implement output channel events and configuration retrieval in CocoonService\n\nReplace stubbed TODO implementations for output channel operations and get_configuration with working implementations:\n\n- **Output Channels (create, append, clear, show, dispose)**: Emit Tauri events to Sky (`sky://output/*`) to notify the frontend to create, update, clear, show, or dispose output panels. This enables the extension host to write to output channels that Sky renders in the editor UI.\n\n- **get_configuration**: Delegate to ConfigurationProvider to retrieve VS Code configuration values. The section and key from the request are combined into a dot-notation key (e.g., \"editor.fontSize\") and passed to GetConfigurationValue. Returns the serialized JSON value.\n\nThese implementations complete the gRPC contract between Mountain and Cocoon, enabling VS Code extensions running in Cocoon to interact with the editor's output panels and configuration system.",
			"SHA": "65a75298bafffa634d230333d1dd72aa60bcb499"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-05T13:38:26Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				670,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): add Wind IPC handlers for terminal, output, and textFile commands\n\nAdd command handlers in WindServiceHandlers to expose terminal, output channel,\nand text file operations to the Wind frontend via Tauri IPC:\n\n- Terminal: create, sendText, dispose, show, hide - delegate to TerminalProvider\n- Output channels: create, append, appendLine, clear, show - emit Tauri events to Sky\n- TextFile: read, write, save - use tokio::fs for disk I/O\n\nThese handlers complete the IPC bridge between Wind's service layer and\nMountain's native backend capabilities.",
			"SHA": "6ed9f10234aa14095301f824fa65e5c31a924349"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-05T13:35:49Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				670,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): implement generic request router in process_mountain_request\n\nImplement the generic request handler that routes fs.* and commands.execute methods from Cocoon's FileSystemService. The previous implementation returned \"Method not found\" errors for all requests.\n\nNow properly handles: fs.readFile/file:read, fs.writeFile/file:write, fs.stat/file:stat, fs.listDir/fs.readdir/file:readdir, fs.createDir/file:mkdir, fs.delete/file:delete, fs.rename/file:move, and commands.execute. Each method delegates to the appropriate handler or returns a JSON-RPC compatible response.\n\nThis enables Cocoon's generic ProcessCocoonRequest RPC to work with the same operations available via typed gRPC methods, completing the gRPC service contract.",
			"SHA": "030b3c73fcb413ef014d1c8cb48a38e533e775b5"
		}
	],
